ifa/issues/055 -- FA does not converge (pass_limit_hit=1 at 52 passes) when a shared set method that builds a fresh set (difference/intersection/union) is called with two or more element types AND its result is chained back into another such call. The single `r = set()` inside the method is one creation site shared by every call site, so its element type becomes self-referential and is re-derived every pass. Fails to compile today with BOXING errors; CPython prints 2/1/2, which is what the check file records, so this flips to PASS when the convergence bug is fixed.
